course: dictionary
lesson: 13080
title: Fidelity: faithful and exact
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Fidelity means being faithful and loyal. A faithful friend keeps their promises and stays true to you, even when it is hard. «Rex waited by the gate every evening for his owner.» Rex's fidelity shows he stays loyal, even when he is alone.
explain: Fidelity has a second meaning: how exactly something copies or follows the original. «The new speakers have high fidelity, so every drum beat sounds real.» Here the sound is copied very closely from the recording. Ask yourself: is someone being loyal, or is something being copied accurately?
explain: Read the clues around the word. Words like promise, loyal or owner point to the first meaning. Words like sound, copy, film or original point to the second. «The film kept close to the fidelity of the novel» shows the film stayed true to the book.
fact: Fidelity means being faithful and loyal to a person, a promise or a belief.
fact: Fidelity also means how exactly something copies or follows the original.
fact: «High-fidelity» sound is clear and very close to the original recording.
fact: «The knight swore fidelity to his queen» means he promised to be loyal to her.
fact: Fidelity is an uncountable noun, so you say «some fidelity», not «a fidelity».
exercise: «Rex waited by the gate every evening. His fidelity never wavered.» What does fidelity mean here? | Being very fast and quick | Being hungry for dinner | Being cross with someone | *Being loyal and faithful
exercise: «The new speakers have high fidelity, so every drum beat sounds real.» What does high fidelity mean? | Sound that is played backwards | Sound that is very loud and rough | *Sound copied very exactly from the original | Sound that stops suddenly
exercise: Which word means the opposite of faithful? | *Disloyal | Faithful | Loyal | True
test: «The film kept close to the fidelity of the novel, with every key scene.» What does fidelity mean here? | Being hungry for a long time | Being loud and bright | *Being exact to the original book | Being sleepy after lunch
test: Mia says fidelity is just a fancy word for being happy. What is a better meaning? | Being rich | *Being faithful and loyal, or being exact to an original | Being happy for a long time | Being very quiet
exam: Which sentence uses fidelity correctly? | *The dog showed great fidelity to his owner. | The fidelity was very hungry and tall. | The fidelities are running fast in the park. | The dog ate fidelity for lunch.
